WEBVTT

00:00:01.507 --> 00:00:04.370
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.604
Goodbye, Mr. Hollywood, by John Escott.

00:00:09.664 --> 00:00:12.618
Read by Danica Fairman.

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:17.862
Published and Copyright, Oxford University Press, 1996.

00:00:17.882 --> 00:00:18.362
Chapter 1.

00:00:18.422 --> 00:00:23.095
Mystery Girl.

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:42.102
It all began on a beautiful spring morning in a village called Whistler in Canada, a pretty little village in the mountains of British Columbia.

00:00:42.162 --> 00:00:53.317
There was a café in the village with tables outside and at one of these tables sat a young man.

00:00:53.377 --> 00:01:06.348
He finished his breakfast drank his coffee, looked up into the blue sky, and felt the warm sun on his face.

00:01:06.408 --> 00:01:11.192
Nick Lortz was a happy man.

00:01:11.252 --> 00:01:14.804
The waiter came up to his table.

00:01:14.864 --> 00:01:16.946
More coffee?

00:01:17.006 --> 00:01:18.556
He asked.

00:01:18.616 --> 00:01:20.938
Yeah, great!

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:22.670
said Nick.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.317
He gave the waiter his coffee cup.

00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:30.845
The waiter looked at the camera on the table.

00:01:30.905 --> 00:01:34.559
On vacation, he said.

00:01:34.618 --> 00:01:37.121
Where are you from?

00:01:37.181 --> 00:01:41.305
San Francisco, Nick said.

00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:43.316
He laughed.

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:46.300
But I'm not on vacation.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.104
I'm working.

00:01:48.164 --> 00:01:54.800
I'm a travel writer, and I'm doing a book on mountains in North America.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.542
I've got some great pictures of your mountain."

00:01:59.602 --> 00:02:05.354
The two men looked up but whistler mountain behind the village.

00:02:05.414 --> 00:02:09.836
It looked very beautiful in the morning sun.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.428
Do you travel a lot then?

00:02:13.487 --> 00:02:15.546
asked the waiter.

00:02:15.606 --> 00:02:18.998
All the time, Nick said.

00:02:19.058 --> 00:02:24.482
I write books, and I write for travel magazines.

00:02:24.542 --> 00:02:27.224
I write about everything.

00:02:27.284 --> 00:02:35.932
Different countries, towns, villages, rivers, mountains, people.

00:02:35.992 --> 00:02:40.004
The waiter looked over Nick's head.

00:02:40.064 --> 00:02:44.939
There's a girl across the street, he said.

00:02:44.999 --> 00:02:47.510
Do you know her?

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.983
Nick turned his head and looked.

00:02:51.042 --> 00:02:53.854
No, I don't.

00:02:53.914 --> 00:02:58.176
Well, she knows you, I think.

00:02:58.236 --> 00:03:00.067
The waiter said.

00:03:00.126 --> 00:03:03.959
She's watching you very carefully.

00:03:04.018 --> 00:03:07.020
He gave Nick a smile.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.442
Have a nice day.

00:03:09.502 --> 00:03:14.856
He went away, back into the cafe.

00:03:14.916 --> 00:03:19.792
Nick looked at the girl across the street.

00:03:19.852 --> 00:03:25.894
She was about twenty-five, and she was very pretty.

00:03:25.954 --> 00:03:31.298
She is watching me, Nick thought.

00:03:31.358 --> 00:03:43.572
Then the girl turned and looked in one of the shop windows After a second or two, she looked back at Nick again.

00:03:43.632 --> 00:03:45.982
Nick watched her.

00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:49.856
She looks worried, he thought.

00:03:49.915 --> 00:03:52.056
What's she doing?

00:03:52.116 --> 00:03:55.669
Is she waiting for somebody?

00:03:55.729 --> 00:03:59.642
Suddenly the girl smiled.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:07.622
Then she walked across the street, came up to Nick's table, and sat down.

00:04:07.682 --> 00:04:11.520
She put her bag down on the table.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.762
The bag was half open.

00:04:14.822 --> 00:04:19.735
Hi, I'm Jan, she said.

00:04:19.795 --> 00:04:22.116
Do you remember me?

00:04:22.176 --> 00:04:26.429
We met at a party in Toronto.

00:04:26.489 --> 00:04:30.092
Hi Jan, said Nick.

00:04:30.152 --> 00:04:32.092
He smiled.

00:04:32.152 --> 00:04:38.053
I'm Nick, but we didn't meet at a party in Toronto.

00:04:38.113 --> 00:04:44.056
I don't go to parties very often and never in Toronto.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:51.798
Oh, the girl said, but she didn't get up or move away.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:55.850
Have some coffee, said Nick.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:05:06.098
The story about the party in Toronto wasn't true, but it was a beautiful morning, and she was a pretty girl.

00:05:06.157 --> 00:05:12.022
Maybe it was a party in Montreal, or New York.

00:05:12.082 --> 00:05:14.414
The girl laughed.

00:05:14.474 --> 00:05:17.766
Okay, maybe it was.

00:05:17.826 --> 00:05:22.148
And yes, I'd love some coffee.

00:05:22.208 --> 00:05:29.620
When she had her coffee, Nick asked, what are you doing in Whistler?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.181
Or do you live here?

00:05:32.241 --> 00:05:35.202
Oh, no, she said.

00:05:35.262 --> 00:05:39.823
I'm just, uh, just traveling through.

00:05:39.843 --> 00:05:44.134
And what are you doing here?

00:05:44.194 --> 00:05:48.266
I'm a travel writer, Nick said.

00:05:48.326 --> 00:05:52.738
And I'm writing a book about famous mountains.

00:05:52.797 --> 00:05:57.131
That's interesting, she said.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:04.456
But her face was worried, not interested, and she looked across the road again.

00:06:04.476 --> 00:06:13.122
A man with very short white hair walked across the road.

00:06:13.182 --> 00:06:19.656
He was about sixty years old, and he was tall and thin.

00:06:19.716 --> 00:06:22.758
The girl watched him.

00:06:22.818 --> 00:06:25.988
Are you waiting for someone?"

00:06:26.048 --> 00:06:28.789
asked Nick.

00:06:28.809 --> 00:06:31.391
No, she said quickly.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:37.694
Then she asked, where are you going next, Nick?

00:06:37.754 --> 00:06:44.436
To Vancouver, for three or four days, he said.

00:06:44.496 --> 00:06:46.718
When are you going?

00:06:46.778 --> 00:06:48.347
She asked.

00:06:48.406 --> 00:06:57.667
Later this morning, he said, there was a letter in the top of the girl's half-open bag.

00:06:57.727 --> 00:07:06.939
Nick could seize some of the writing, and he read it because he saw the word Vancouver.

00:07:06.999 --> 00:07:24.602
And we can meet at the Empress Hotel, Victoria, Vancouver Island on Friday afternoon, So she's going to Vancouver too, he thought.

00:07:24.662 --> 00:07:30.384
Suddenly the girl said, Do you like movies?

00:07:30.444 --> 00:07:32.015
Movies?

00:07:32.075 --> 00:07:34.856
Yes, I love movies.

00:07:34.916 --> 00:07:37.037
He said, Why?

00:07:37.057 --> 00:07:44.360
I know a man and he loves movies.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:50.614
And going to the cinema, she said slowly.

00:07:50.674 --> 00:07:55.476
People call him Mr. Hollywood.

00:07:55.536 --> 00:07:58.296
She smiled at Nick.

00:07:58.356 --> 00:08:03.248
Can I call you Mr. Hollywood too?

00:08:03.308 --> 00:08:05.509
Nick laughed.

00:08:05.569 --> 00:08:08.500
Okay, he said.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:12.431
And what can I call you?

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:15.107
She smiled again.

00:08:15.167 --> 00:08:19.503
"'Call me, mystery girl,' she said.

00:08:19.523 --> 00:08:25.524
"'That's a good name for you,' said Nick.

00:08:25.584 --> 00:08:32.185
Just then, the man with white hair came into the cafe.

00:08:32.246 --> 00:08:40.154
He did not look at Nick or the girl, but he sat at a table near them.

00:08:40.213 --> 00:08:43.771
He asked the waiter for some breakfast.

00:08:43.831 --> 00:08:47.922
Then he began to read a magazine.

00:08:47.982 --> 00:08:54.464
The girl looked the man, then quickly looked away again.

00:08:54.524 --> 00:08:56.654
Do you know him?

00:08:56.714 --> 00:08:59.625
Nick asked her.

00:08:59.645 --> 00:09:01.575
No, she said.

00:09:01.635 --> 00:09:05.876
She finished her coffee quickly and got up.

00:09:05.936 --> 00:09:09.646
I must go now, she said.

00:09:09.706 --> 00:09:12.256
Nick stood up, too.

00:09:12.316 --> 00:09:15.639
Nice to—he began.

00:09:15.699 --> 00:09:24.136
But the girl suddenly took his face between her hands and kissed him on the mouth.

00:09:24.195 --> 00:09:28.829
Drive carefully, Mr. Hollywood!

00:09:28.889 --> 00:09:30.590
Good-bye!

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:35.724
She said, with a big, beautiful smile.

00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:41.312
Then she turned and walked quickly away.

00:09:41.372 --> 00:09:46.770
Nick sat down again and watched her.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:52.294
She walked down the road and into a big hotel.

00:09:52.354 --> 00:09:59.389
Now what, thought Nick, was that all about?

00:09:59.449 --> 00:10:06.264
The man with white hair watched Nick and waited.

00:10:06.324 --> 00:10:18.145
After four or five minutes, Nick finished his coffee took his books and his camera, and left the cafe.

00:10:18.205 --> 00:10:27.648
His car was just outside the girl's hotel, and he walked slowly along the street to it.

00:10:27.708 --> 00:10:36.392
The man with white hair waited a second, then quickly followed Nick.

00:10:36.452 --> 00:10:45.242
From a window High up in the hotel, the girl looked down into the road.

00:10:45.302 --> 00:10:53.420
She saw Nick and the man with white hair about fifty yards behind him.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:11:03.690
Nick got into his car and the man with white hair walked quickly to a red car across the street.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:14.154
Five seconds later, Nick drove away in his blue car, and the red car began to follow him.

00:11:14.214 --> 00:11:24.196
When the girl saw this, she smiled, then went to put some things in her travel bag.

00:11:24.256 --> 00:11:42.072
CHAPTER II A HAND IN THE BACK That evening, in his hotel room in Vancouver, Nick could not stop thinking about the girl in the Whistler Cafe.

00:11:42.132 --> 00:11:45.943
Why did she come and sit with him?

00:11:46.003 --> 00:11:57.538
She didn't know him, and that story about a party in Toronto wasn't true, and she was worried about something.

00:11:57.598 --> 00:11:59.943
But what?

00:12:00.003 --> 00:12:02.799
and that kiss.

00:12:02.859 --> 00:12:05.800
It was nice, of course.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:08.702
But why did she do it?

00:12:08.762 --> 00:12:11.804
Maybe she liked my face.

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:13.375
Nick thought.

00:12:13.435 --> 00:12:15.866
Or my brown eyes.

00:12:15.926 --> 00:12:19.138
But I'm not going to see her again.

00:12:19.198 --> 00:12:21.360
So it doesn't matter.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.931
Forget it.

00:12:23.991 --> 00:12:31.988
He put some money in his pocket and went downstairs to the hotel restaurant.

00:12:32.048 --> 00:12:41.976
But there were no free tables, so he walked down to Gastown and found a restaurant there.

00:12:42.036 --> 00:12:46.853
After dinner, he went for a walk.

00:12:46.913 --> 00:12:59.829
Vancouver was a friendly city, and Nick liked walking through Gastown and Chinatown, looking in the shops and watching the people.

00:12:59.889 --> 00:13:06.376
It was nearly dark now, and it was a busy time of the evening.

00:13:06.436 --> 00:13:12.147
There were a lot of cars and a lot of people.

00:13:12.206 --> 00:13:18.417
After a time, Nick began to walk back to his hotel.

00:13:18.477 --> 00:13:26.244
He came to a busy street and waited with a small crowd of people to go across.

00:13:26.304 --> 00:13:31.538
A tall woman in a blue dress stood next to him.

00:13:31.598 --> 00:13:35.236
She turned and smiled at him.

00:13:35.296 --> 00:13:40.976
It's the first warm evening of spring," she said.

00:13:41.036 --> 00:13:46.100
It's nice to be out after the long cold winter.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.902
Yeah, said Nick.

00:13:48.962 --> 00:13:50.373
It's great.

00:13:50.434 --> 00:14:00.712
It's suddenly there was a hand in his back, and the hand pushed Nick into the road.

00:14:00.772 --> 00:14:06.956
Nick fell on his face in front of a big, green car.

00:14:07.016 --> 00:14:09.816
People screamed.

00:14:09.876 --> 00:14:15.817
But the green car stopped only inches from Nick's head.

00:14:15.877 --> 00:14:22.768
The woman in the blue dress ran into the road and pulled Nick to his feet.

00:14:22.788 --> 00:14:25.799
Her, you okay?

00:14:25.859 --> 00:14:27.249
What happened?

00:14:27.309 --> 00:14:28.890
She said.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:37.804
The driver of the green car shouted angrily at Nick, but Nick did not hear him.

00:14:37.864 --> 00:14:42.508
Somebody pushed me, he said to the woman.

00:14:42.568 --> 00:14:44.630
I didn't fall.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.602
Somebody pushed me.

00:14:47.662 --> 00:14:51.616
Pushed you, said the woman.

00:14:51.636 --> 00:14:55.779
I didn't see anybody.

00:14:55.839 --> 00:15:02.880
Nick looked at the faces of the people near him, but he didn't know them.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:06.668
Then he saw a man's back.

00:15:06.728 --> 00:15:13.652
The man was tall and thin, and had very short, white hair.

00:15:13.712 --> 00:15:20.818
He walked quickly away, down the street, and did not look back.

00:15:20.878 --> 00:15:23.830
Hey, you!

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:26.922
Nick shouted, wait!

00:15:26.982 --> 00:15:36.548
But the man did not stop, and he was soon lost in the crowds Did he push you?

00:15:36.608 --> 00:15:40.752
asked the woman in the blue dress.

00:15:40.772 --> 00:15:45.766
I don't know, Nick said.

00:15:45.826 --> 00:15:48.188
Do you know him?

00:15:48.248 --> 00:15:50.250
She asked.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:54.702
I don't know his name, Nick said.

00:15:54.762 --> 00:15:58.686
But I know that short white hair.

00:15:58.746 --> 00:16:03.752
Now where did I see it before?

00:16:03.812 --> 00:16:08.418
The woman began to move away.

00:16:08.478 --> 00:16:12.602
I must get home, she said.

00:16:12.662 --> 00:16:15.444
Are you okay now?

00:16:15.504 --> 00:16:20.168
Yeah, I'm okay, Nick said.

00:16:20.228 --> 00:16:22.090
And thanks.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:24.923
Thanks for your help.

00:16:24.983 --> 00:16:29.608
That's okay, the woman smiled.

00:16:29.668 --> 00:16:33.020
Be careful now.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:40.783
Back in his hotel, Nick sat on his bed and thought.

00:16:40.843 --> 00:16:44.144
It was an accident.

00:16:44.204 --> 00:16:46.685
Nobody pushed me.

00:16:46.744 --> 00:16:49.455
It was an accident.

00:16:49.515 --> 00:16:58.216
Nobody wants to kill me, and there are hundreds of men in Vancouver with white hair.

00:16:58.276 --> 00:17:05.046
It was one o'clock in the morning, but Nick couldn't sleep.

00:17:05.107 --> 00:17:14.292
He listened to the cars in the road, and he looked at the night sky through his hotel room window.

00:17:14.352 --> 00:17:22.278
Then he sat at the table and tried to write some more of his book about mountains.

00:17:22.339 --> 00:17:25.862
But he couldn't think about his work.

00:17:25.922 --> 00:17:29.614
He got back into bed.

00:17:29.674 --> 00:17:35.464
There were four or five magazines in the hotel room.

00:17:35.524 --> 00:17:48.066
They were not very interesting, but Nick sat in bed and opened one, and saw a photo of Mystery Girl.

00:17:48.126 --> 00:17:57.220
He looked at the picture very carefully, but, yes, it was her.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:14.926
Jan, the girl from the Whistler Cafe, She was next to a man of about fifty or fifty-five, and they were in the garden of a big, expensive house.

00:18:14.986 --> 00:18:21.330
They smiled at the camera, and they looked very happy.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:31.425
Canadian millionaire Howard Hudson and his daughter Meg, it said, under the picture.

00:18:31.486 --> 00:18:35.219
at their home in Toronto.

00:18:35.279 --> 00:18:47.039
Meg Hudson, not Jan, not Mystery Girl, Meg Hudson, the daughter of a millionaire.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:50.602
Nick read it again.

00:18:50.663 --> 00:18:57.028
Why did she come and sit with me in the cafe at Whistler?

00:18:57.088 --> 00:18:58.544
He thought.

00:18:58.604 --> 00:19:07.778
Millionaire's daughters don't sit with strangers in cafes, and then give them a big kiss when they leave.

00:19:07.838 --> 00:19:10.300
Why did she do it?

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:13.463
What did she want?

00:19:13.523 --> 00:19:21.090
He thought back to the cafe in Wesler, and the girl next to him at the table.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:24.690
Then he remembered something.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:30.321
He remembered a man at a table near them in the cafe.

00:19:30.381 --> 00:19:35.485
A tall, thin man, about sixty years old.

00:19:35.505 --> 00:19:41.620
A man with very short, white hair.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:47.266
Nick didn't sleep much that night.

00:19:47.326 --> 00:19:54.428
Chapter 3 A walk in the park.

00:19:54.488 --> 00:19:58.738
The next day was Thursday.

00:19:58.798 --> 00:20:05.582
Nick stayed in his hotel room and rode about mountains all morning.

00:20:05.642 --> 00:20:11.214
Then he drove to Stanley Park in the afternoon.

00:20:11.274 --> 00:20:15.336
He sat and read a book for an hour.

00:20:15.396 --> 00:20:20.803
Then he went for a walk under the tall trees.

00:20:20.863 --> 00:20:23.817
There was nobody here.

00:20:23.878 --> 00:20:29.409
It was quiet, and he could walk and think.

00:20:29.469 --> 00:20:36.510
He thought about Meg Hudson and about the man with white hair.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:40.182
Did he know Meg Hudson?

00:20:40.242 --> 00:20:43.182
Did she know him?

00:20:43.242 --> 00:20:53.596
He remembered Meg Hudson's last words Drive carefully, Mr. Hollywood.

00:20:53.656 --> 00:20:57.768
Why did she say that?

00:20:57.828 --> 00:21:02.682
Why did she call him Mr. Hollywood?

00:21:02.742 --> 00:21:06.724
He didn't understand any of it.

00:21:06.784 --> 00:21:10.876
Suddenly, he heard a noise.

00:21:10.936 --> 00:21:12.918
He stopped.

00:21:12.978 --> 00:21:16.534
That was a gun, he thought.

00:21:16.594 --> 00:21:21.719
There's somebody in the trees with a gun.

00:21:21.779 --> 00:21:24.619
There it is again.

00:21:24.679 --> 00:21:29.560
Then something hit the tree over his head.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:32.661
Somebody's shooting at me.

00:21:32.721 --> 00:21:34.431
Nick thought.

00:21:34.491 --> 00:21:37.552
He turned and ran.

00:21:37.612 --> 00:21:42.322
And somebody began to run after him.

00:21:42.382 --> 00:21:46.154
Nick ran through the trees.

00:21:46.214 --> 00:21:51.246
There was no sun in here, and it was half dark.

00:21:51.306 --> 00:21:56.848
And there were no people, nobody to help him.

00:21:56.908 --> 00:22:01.820
I must get to my car, Nick thought.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:06.162
Find some people, the police.

00:22:06.222 --> 00:22:09.142
He ran on.

00:22:09.202 --> 00:22:16.077
He could still hear the gunman behind him, so he ran faster.

00:22:16.137 --> 00:22:22.432
After three or four minutes, he stopped and listened.

00:22:22.492 --> 00:22:24.774
Nothing.

00:22:24.834 --> 00:22:28.296
It was all quiet.

00:22:28.356 --> 00:22:31.617
Nick was afraid.

00:22:31.678 --> 00:22:33.538
What's happening?

00:22:33.598 --> 00:22:35.029
He thought.

00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:38.950
Why is somebody shooting at me?

00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:48.731
First a hand pushes me in front of a car, and now somebody's shooting at me.

00:22:48.791 --> 00:22:57.032
He waited another second or two, then walked quickly back to his car.

00:22:57.092 --> 00:22:59.803
He was very careful.

00:22:59.863 --> 00:23:04.197
He looked and listened all the time.

00:23:04.257 --> 00:23:10.963
But nobody came out of the trees, and nobody shot at him.

00:23:11.024 --> 00:23:14.174
Then he saw people.

00:23:14.234 --> 00:23:19.808
Women with young children, some boys with a football.

00:23:19.868 --> 00:23:22.840
Two men with a dog.

00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:26.032
He began to feel better.

00:23:26.092 --> 00:23:30.434
Nobody can shoot me now, he thought.

00:23:30.494 --> 00:23:34.453
Not with all these people here.

00:23:34.514 --> 00:23:40.494
Ten minutes later, he was back at his car.

00:23:40.554 --> 00:23:43.926
There was a ladder on the window.

00:23:43.986 --> 00:23:46.068
Nick read it.

00:23:46.128 --> 00:23:53.932
It said, I'm going to kill you, Mr. Hollywood.

00:23:53.992 --> 00:23:58.984
Nick drove to the nearest police station.

00:23:59.044 --> 00:24:02.204
He waited for half an hour.

00:24:02.264 --> 00:24:08.516
Then a tired young policeman took him into a small room.

00:24:08.576 --> 00:24:15.518
Nick told his story, and the policeman wrote it all down.

00:24:15.577 --> 00:24:19.709
So, what are you going to do?

00:24:19.769 --> 00:24:22.370
asked Nick.

00:24:22.430 --> 00:24:27.493
Nothing, said the policeman.

00:24:27.553 --> 00:24:31.087
Nothing, said Nick.

00:24:31.147 --> 00:24:46.208
But somebody shot at me and, Mr. Lord's, the policeman said, tiredly, how many people are there in this town with guns?

00:24:46.268 --> 00:24:53.974
I don't know, said Nick, but you didn't see the gun man.

00:24:54.034 --> 00:25:00.484
Was it a man, a boy, a woman, Color of eyes?

00:25:00.544 --> 00:25:01.845
Long hair?

00:25:01.905 --> 00:25:03.246
Short hair?

00:25:03.306 --> 00:25:08.430
You don't know, because you didn't see anybody.

00:25:08.490 --> 00:25:12.222
Maybe it was an old girlfriend.

00:25:12.282 --> 00:25:18.166
Maybe somebody doesn't like your travel books, Mr. Lord's.

00:25:18.226 --> 00:25:25.543
But what about the man with white hair in Whistler, said Nick?

00:25:25.603 --> 00:25:32.340
The girl, Meg Hudson, called me Mr. Hollywood in the cafe.

00:25:32.400 --> 00:25:35.172
And this man heard her.

00:25:35.232 --> 00:25:42.246
And now I get a letter to Mr. Hollywood on my car.

00:25:42.306 --> 00:25:46.508
Who is this Mr. Hollywood?

00:25:46.568 --> 00:25:53.898
We all want answers to our questions, Mr. Lord's, the policeman said.

00:25:53.959 --> 00:25:57.875
But we don't always get them."

00:25:57.935 --> 00:26:00.146
Questions.

00:26:00.206 --> 00:26:03.776
But no answers.

00:26:03.836 --> 00:26:10.298
Nick walked out of the police station and drove to his hotel.

00:26:10.358 --> 00:26:14.188
He was angry and afraid.

00:26:14.249 --> 00:26:19.870
How did the man with white hair find me in Vancouver?

00:26:19.930 --> 00:26:21.231
He thought.

00:26:21.290 --> 00:26:24.448
Did he follow me from Whistler?

00:26:24.508 --> 00:26:27.774
Is he following me now?

00:26:27.835 --> 00:26:37.737
Maybe he's staying at my hotel, too, in the next room, with his gun.

00:26:37.797 --> 00:26:50.641
Chapter 4 The Man With White Hair Nick stopped his car in front of the hotel.

00:26:50.701 --> 00:26:58.956
He looked carefully before he got out, but there was nobody with white hair near the hotel.

00:26:59.016 --> 00:27:06.440
He half ran through the hotel doors and went to the desk inside.

00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:14.723
I'm looking for a man with very short white hair, he said to the woman behind the desk.

00:27:14.783 --> 00:27:17.494
He's staying here, I think.

00:27:17.554 --> 00:27:20.922
He's about sixty years old.

00:27:20.982 --> 00:27:24.200
And he's tall and thin.

00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:28.834
The woman did not look very interested.

00:27:28.894 --> 00:27:35.160
There are a lot of visitors in the hotel, she said.

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:37.802
Do you know his name?

00:27:37.862 --> 00:27:41.716
No, I don't, Nick said.

00:27:41.776 --> 00:27:46.938
He's a friend of a friend, you see.

00:27:46.998 --> 00:27:53.090
He arrived in Vancouver yesterday, and I must find him.

00:27:53.150 --> 00:27:55.602
It's very important.

00:27:55.662 --> 00:27:58.464
Please help me."

00:27:58.524 --> 00:28:02.176
The woman looked at him.

00:28:02.236 --> 00:28:14.346
There are 350 rooms in this hotel, she said, and maybe 30 or 40 men with white hair.

00:28:14.406 --> 00:28:18.033
How can I remember all their names?

00:28:18.093 --> 00:28:22.441
She turned away to answer a telephone call.

00:28:22.501 --> 00:28:26.604
Nick walked away from the desk.

00:28:26.664 --> 00:28:29.836
A drink, he thought.

00:28:29.896 --> 00:28:32.539
I need a drink.

00:28:32.599 --> 00:28:40.145
He went into the hotel bar, got a drink, and sat down at a table.

00:28:40.205 --> 00:28:44.318
So, what do I do now?

00:28:44.378 --> 00:28:46.536
He thought.

00:28:46.596 --> 00:28:51.136
And then he remembered something.

00:28:51.196 --> 00:28:58.620
A letter in the girl's half-open bag in the Whistler Cafe.

00:28:58.680 --> 00:29:10.008
And we can meet at the Empress Hotel, Victoria, Vancouver Island on Friday afternoon.

00:29:10.067 --> 00:29:14.798
And tomorrow was Friday.

00:29:14.858 --> 00:29:25.958
I'm going to Victoria on Vancouver Island," he thought, to the Empress Hotel.

00:29:26.019 --> 00:29:31.560
Nick had dinner in the hotel that evening.

00:29:31.620 --> 00:29:41.147
He finished eating and got up from his table and saw the man with white hair.

00:29:41.207 --> 00:29:44.323
Nick moved quickly.

00:29:44.383 --> 00:29:47.684
The man was at the hotel desk.

00:29:47.744 --> 00:29:55.884
Nick could see the white head above the other heads near the desk.

00:29:55.944 --> 00:30:02.334
He pushed past the people in the hotel restaurant.

00:30:02.394 --> 00:30:08.178
A small boy ran in front of him, and Nick ran into him.

00:30:08.238 --> 00:30:12.140
The boy and Nick fell down on the floor.

00:30:12.201 --> 00:30:14.830
The boy began to cry.

00:30:14.890 --> 00:30:16.368
Hey!

00:30:16.428 --> 00:30:18.730
said a woman behind Nick.

00:30:18.790 --> 00:30:22.022
I'm very sorry, said Nick.

00:30:22.082 --> 00:30:25.604
He got up and helped the boy to his feet.

00:30:25.664 --> 00:30:27.216
Are you okay?

00:30:27.276 --> 00:30:28.998
He asked the boy.

00:30:29.058 --> 00:30:34.011
Be more careful next time, said the woman.

00:30:34.071 --> 00:30:37.144
Nick moved away quickly.

00:30:37.204 --> 00:30:44.058
But when he looked back at the hotel desk, he couldn't see the man with white hair.

00:30:44.118 --> 00:30:48.080
He pushed through the crowd of people.

00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:53.884
That man, he shouted at the woman behind the desk.

00:30:53.944 --> 00:30:58.008
That man with short white hair.

00:30:58.068 --> 00:30:59.729
Where did he go?

00:30:59.749 --> 00:31:03.832
The woman looked at Nick.

00:31:03.892 --> 00:31:07.474
Mr. Vickers, she said.

00:31:07.534 --> 00:31:08.895
I don't know.

00:31:08.915 --> 00:31:11.662
Vickers.

00:31:11.722 --> 00:31:14.000
"'Is that his name?'

00:31:14.060 --> 00:31:15.612
said Nick.

00:31:15.672 --> 00:31:17.534
"'What's his room number?'

00:31:17.554 --> 00:31:20.156
"'I'm sorry.

00:31:20.176 --> 00:31:23.839
I can't tell you that,' the woman said.

00:31:23.859 --> 00:31:28.654
"'But I need to,' began Nick.

00:31:28.714 --> 00:31:33.538
The woman turned away to answer the telephone.

00:31:33.598 --> 00:31:39.986
After a second or two, Nick went upstairs to his room.

00:31:40.046 --> 00:31:43.150
Vickers, he thought.

00:31:43.210 --> 00:31:47.940
Does Meg Hudson know, Mr. Vickers?

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:55.612
I need some answers, and I need them quickly.

00:31:55.672 --> 00:32:08.428
Chapter 5 Vancouver Island Tawassen was about 23 miles south of Vancouver.

00:32:08.488 --> 00:32:17.213
Nick drove there in his car the next morning for the one o'clock ferry to Vancouver Island.

00:32:17.274 --> 00:32:21.935
Every five minutes he looked behind him.

00:32:21.995 --> 00:32:24.646
The road was busy.

00:32:24.706 --> 00:32:31.329
Black cars, white cars, red cars, green cars.

00:32:31.389 --> 00:32:35.374
Maybe Vickers was in one of them.

00:32:35.434 --> 00:32:42.302
At Tawasan, Nick drove his car onto the ferry.

00:32:42.362 --> 00:32:48.096
There were a lot of cars and crowds of people.

00:32:48.156 --> 00:32:55.350
Nick got out of his car and walked up and down the ship.

00:32:55.410 --> 00:33:01.892
He looked for a man with white hair, but he didn't see one.

00:33:01.952 --> 00:33:08.466
Soon the ferry began to move and Nick felt better.

00:33:08.526 --> 00:33:14.740
He found the ferry restaurant and got something to eat.

00:33:14.800 --> 00:33:17.991
More people came in.

00:33:18.052 --> 00:33:23.234
Nick looked at the faces of all the older men.

00:33:23.294 --> 00:33:30.628
Some had hats on, so he looked for somebody tall and thin.

00:33:30.688 --> 00:33:33.634
But there was nobody.

00:33:33.694 --> 00:33:38.862
Maybe he's not on the ferry, Nick thought.

00:33:38.922 --> 00:33:43.156
Maybe he's back in Vancouver.

00:33:43.216 --> 00:33:48.540
Later, Nick walked around the ship again.

00:33:48.600 --> 00:33:58.332
Once, he thought he saw the man with white hair in the crowds, but he could not be sure.

00:33:58.392 --> 00:34:13.150
90 minutes after leaving Tawasan, the ferry arrived at Swartz Bay on Vancouver Island and Nick went back down to his car.

00:34:13.210 --> 00:34:20.481
Swartz Bay was 20 miles north of Victoria.

00:34:20.541 --> 00:34:36.554
Nick drove quickly and again looked behind him every four or five minutes Once, he saw a red car about two hundred yards behind him.

00:34:36.614 --> 00:34:42.518
Did I see that car on the road from Vancouver to Tawassen?

00:34:42.578 --> 00:34:44.519
He thought.

00:34:44.579 --> 00:34:53.204
He drove more slowly, but the red car still stayed two hundred yards behind him.

00:34:53.265 --> 00:35:00.108
And Nick couldn't see the driver's face or hair.

00:35:00.168 --> 00:35:11.576
Soon he was in the busy streets of Victoria, and Nick didn't see the red car behind him again.

00:35:11.636 --> 00:35:19.421
Victoria was a city of gardens and beautiful old buildings.

00:35:19.481 --> 00:35:38.682
Nick liked Victoria very much, but today he wasn't interested in gardens or buildings He found the Empress Hotel, went inside, and walked across to the desk.

00:35:38.743 --> 00:35:41.224
Can I help you?

00:35:41.284 --> 00:35:44.366
A young man asked Nick.

00:35:44.426 --> 00:35:50.448
I'm meeting a friend here this afternoon, said Nick.

00:35:50.508 --> 00:35:52.970
Miss Hudson.

00:35:53.030 --> 00:35:56.962
Hudson, said the young man.

00:35:57.022 --> 00:35:59.051
Wait a minute.

00:35:59.111 --> 00:36:02.430
He went away and came back.

00:36:02.490 --> 00:36:08.610
Sorry, but there's no Miss Hudson staying here.

00:36:08.670 --> 00:36:12.851
Nick took something from his pocket.

00:36:12.912 --> 00:36:20.193
It was the photograph of Meg and her father from the magazine.

00:36:20.253 --> 00:36:24.174
This is her, he said.

00:36:24.234 --> 00:36:28.358
The young man looked at the picture.

00:36:28.418 --> 00:36:30.792
Oh, right!

00:36:30.852 --> 00:36:35.406
You mean Howard Hudson's daughter," he said.

00:36:35.466 --> 00:36:41.592
She's not staying here, but I saw her ten or fifteen minutes ago.

00:36:41.652 --> 00:36:43.624
She was with somebody.

00:36:43.644 --> 00:36:45.476
A man.

00:36:45.536 --> 00:36:49.058
He asked me about the tea room.

00:36:49.118 --> 00:36:52.422
The tea room, said Nick.

00:36:52.482 --> 00:36:55.648
Where's that?

00:36:55.708 --> 00:37:02.236
The man with short white hair was tired.

00:37:02.296 --> 00:37:06.598
He couldn't sleep, and he couldn't eat.

00:37:06.658 --> 00:37:12.451
He thought about only one thing, all the time.

00:37:12.511 --> 00:37:19.574
He drove, and he watched, and he waited, and he followed.

00:37:19.634 --> 00:37:31.068
When he drove into Victoria, the streets were busy, and suddenly he lost the blue car in front of him.

00:37:31.129 --> 00:37:39.262
Angrily he drove around the city, past all the big hotels.

00:37:39.322 --> 00:37:43.826
I must find him, he said.

00:37:43.886 --> 00:37:48.274
I must do it, today.

00:37:48.334 --> 00:37:58.518
Then he saw the Empress Hotel and in the street outside it a blue car.

00:37:58.578 --> 00:38:07.968
He drove past the hotel, left his car and ran back down the street.

00:38:08.028 --> 00:38:14.719
He went across the road and walked past the downstairs windows.

00:38:14.779 --> 00:38:21.470
There was a big room with tables and chairs, and a lot of people.

00:38:21.530 --> 00:38:26.024
He looked carefully at all the faces.

00:38:26.084 --> 00:38:30.558
There she is, he said suddenly.

00:38:30.618 --> 00:38:34.240
There were two men with the girl.

00:38:34.301 --> 00:38:44.134
He couldn't see their faces, only the backs of their heads, but one of the men was in a green shirt.

00:38:44.194 --> 00:38:50.342
Mr. Hollywood, the man said and smiled.

00:38:50.402 --> 00:38:55.034
Goodbye, Mr. Hollywood.

00:38:55.094 --> 00:39:02.478
People in the street turned to look at him, but the man did not see them.

00:39:02.538 --> 00:39:10.812
He walked up to the doors of the hotel and put a hand into his pocket.

00:39:10.872 --> 00:39:18.567
Inside, the gun was cold and hard.

00:39:18.628 --> 00:39:33.366
CHAPTER VI A TEA PARTY Nick looked through the doors of the tea-room in the Empress Hotel.

00:39:33.426 --> 00:39:38.269
Meg Hudson sat at a table with a man.

00:39:38.329 --> 00:39:44.872
The man was about thirty, or maybe a year or two younger.

00:39:44.932 --> 00:39:49.746
He was tall and brown from the sun.

00:39:49.806 --> 00:39:56.930
He wore a white shirt, white trousers, and white shoes.

00:39:56.991 --> 00:40:01.494
He said something to Meg, and she laughed.

00:40:01.554 --> 00:40:05.166
She looked very happy.

00:40:05.226 --> 00:40:09.280
A waiter came up to Nick.

00:40:09.340 --> 00:40:12.074
Can I get you some tea?"

00:40:12.134 --> 00:40:13.884
he asked.

00:40:13.944 --> 00:40:17.246
No thanks, said Nick.

00:40:17.306 --> 00:40:24.991
I'm with the two people over there, and he walked across to Meg's table.

00:40:25.051 --> 00:40:30.504
Hello, mystery girl, said Nick.

00:40:30.564 --> 00:40:32.776
Remember me?

00:40:32.836 --> 00:40:35.264
We met at Whistler.

00:40:35.324 --> 00:40:43.492
Your name was Jan then, but maybe today it's Meg Hudson.

00:40:43.553 --> 00:40:47.584
Meg Hudson looked up at him.

00:40:47.644 --> 00:40:53.606
Oh, she said, and her face went red.

00:40:53.667 --> 00:40:56.567
Who is this, Meg?

00:40:56.627 --> 00:40:58.498
asked the man.

00:40:58.558 --> 00:41:02.360
This is Nick, said Meg.

00:41:02.420 --> 00:41:04.562
He's a writer.

00:41:04.622 --> 00:41:09.455
Nick, this is Craig Winters.

00:41:09.515 --> 00:41:14.407
Sometimes called Mr. Hollywood?

00:41:14.467 --> 00:41:17.569
Said Nick.

00:41:17.589 --> 00:41:18.199
Maybe.

00:41:18.259 --> 00:41:21.530
But how did you know that?

00:41:21.590 --> 00:41:24.592
Asked Craig Winters.

00:41:24.652 --> 00:41:27.984
I guessed, said Nick.

00:41:28.044 --> 00:41:32.542
And I think I'm beginning to understand.

00:41:32.602 --> 00:41:37.312
Can I ask you a question, Mr. Winters?

00:41:37.372 --> 00:41:41.327
Does somebody want to kill you?

00:41:41.387 --> 00:41:46.082
Craig Winters' face went white.

00:41:46.142 --> 00:41:49.156
Kill me!

00:41:49.216 --> 00:41:53.700
What are you talking about?

00:41:53.761 --> 00:42:01.402
Before I tell you, answer this question, please, said Nick.

00:42:01.462 --> 00:42:06.934
You called me, Mr. Hollywood, in Whistler.

00:42:06.994 --> 00:42:14.916
And you wanted the man at the next table, the man with white hair, to hear you.

00:42:14.976 --> 00:42:17.586
Is that right?

00:42:17.647 --> 00:42:22.373
Meg Hudson did not answer at first.

00:42:22.434 --> 00:42:27.593
Then she said quietly, Yes.

00:42:27.653 --> 00:42:29.354
Why?

00:42:29.414 --> 00:42:31.216
asked Nick.

00:42:31.276 --> 00:42:36.500
I wanted him to follow you, and not me.

00:42:36.560 --> 00:42:38.322
Why?

00:42:38.382 --> 00:42:41.034
Nick asked again.

00:42:41.094 --> 00:42:45.958
I think he's a detective, said Meg.

00:42:46.018 --> 00:42:54.118
And I think he's working for my father I saw him soon after I left Toronto.

00:42:54.178 --> 00:42:56.358
He followed me.

00:42:56.418 --> 00:43:01.190
Meg put her hand on Craig Winter's arm.

00:43:01.250 --> 00:43:04.610
My father doesn't like Craig.

00:43:04.670 --> 00:43:10.001
A month ago, he told me not to see Craig again.

00:43:10.061 --> 00:43:13.952
I'm not happy, and he knows that.

00:43:14.012 --> 00:43:23.866
I think he guessed that I'm meeting Craig And now he wants to find Craig and stop him seeing me.

00:43:23.926 --> 00:43:29.048
Stop him, said Nick, or kill him.

00:43:29.108 --> 00:43:33.989
No, Meg Hudson said, Daddy doesn't.

00:43:34.049 --> 00:43:42.191
The man with white hair pushed me in front of a car in Vancouver, Nick told her.

00:43:42.251 --> 00:43:45.986
And he shot at me in Stanley Park.

00:43:46.046 --> 00:43:48.991
What, said Meg?

00:43:49.051 --> 00:43:55.313
Tell, tell me about this man with white hair?

00:43:55.373 --> 00:43:58.094
Winter said suddenly.

00:43:58.154 --> 00:44:00.615
Nick looked at him.

00:44:00.675 --> 00:44:07.678
He's about sixty, and he's tall and thin, he said.

00:44:07.738 --> 00:44:10.518
Do you know his name?

00:44:10.578 --> 00:44:12.449
asked Winter's.

00:44:12.509 --> 00:44:16.001
Vickers, said Nick.

00:44:16.061 --> 00:44:20.134
Craig Winters suddenly looked ill.

00:44:20.194 --> 00:44:26.806
Did he, did he follow you to Victoria?

00:44:26.866 --> 00:44:29.007
Did he follow you here?

00:44:29.027 --> 00:44:33.348
I don't know, said Nick.

00:44:33.408 --> 00:44:36.200
He watched Winters.

00:44:36.260 --> 00:44:38.901
You're afraid of him?

00:44:38.961 --> 00:44:40.871
Why?

00:44:40.932 --> 00:44:47.732
Why does this man, Vicars, want to kill you, Winters?

00:44:47.792 --> 00:44:54.466
Before Craig Winters could answer, Meg's face went white.

00:44:54.526 --> 00:44:56.118
Oh no!

00:44:56.178 --> 00:44:58.760
She said, look!

00:44:58.820 --> 00:45:00.802
Look over there!

00:45:00.862 --> 00:45:03.148
By the door!

00:45:03.208 --> 00:45:08.564
Nick and Craig Winters turned to look.

00:45:08.624 --> 00:45:14.226
At the door of the tea-room stood the man with white hair.

00:45:14.286 --> 00:45:24.411
He looked up and down the room, and then he saw them, and began to walk across to their table.

00:45:24.471 --> 00:45:28.442
His hand was in his pocket.

00:45:28.502 --> 00:45:35.473
For a second or two, the three people at the table did not move.

00:45:35.533 --> 00:45:40.346
Then Craig Winters jumped to his feet.

00:45:40.406 --> 00:45:43.808
That's Mr. Hollywood!

00:45:43.868 --> 00:45:48.361
He screamed, that man there!

00:45:48.421 --> 00:45:52.794
And he pointed at Nick.

00:45:52.854 --> 00:46:04.418
The man's hand came out of his pocket, with a gun This is for Anna!"

00:46:04.478 --> 00:46:06.698
he shouted.

00:46:06.758 --> 00:46:11.070
Nick moved very fast.

00:46:11.130 --> 00:46:19.304
The tea-table went over, and Nick was down on the floor in a second.

00:46:19.364 --> 00:46:25.756
The shot went over his head, and Meg screamed.

00:46:25.816 --> 00:46:33.835
At the same time, Craig Winters shouted out, and put a hand on his arm.

00:46:33.895 --> 00:46:38.036
There was blood on his white shirt.

00:46:38.096 --> 00:46:48.638
Then more people began to scream, and two waiters pulled the man with white hair down onto the floor.

00:46:48.698 --> 00:46:51.408
Get the police!

00:46:51.468 --> 00:46:55.985
Somebody shouted.

00:46:56.045 --> 00:47:01.942
at the police station.

00:47:02.002 --> 00:47:06.254
It was 730 p.m.

00:47:06.314 --> 00:47:11.406
Nick and Meg were in a room at the police station.

00:47:11.466 --> 00:47:18.317
The man called Vickers was in a different room with three detectives.

00:47:18.377 --> 00:47:22.018
There was a doctor with him too.

00:47:22.078 --> 00:47:26.600
Craig Winters was at the hospital.

00:47:26.660 --> 00:47:33.813
The door opened, and the detective came in with two cups of coffee.

00:47:33.873 --> 00:47:39.486
He put them down on the table, and turned to go out again.

00:47:39.546 --> 00:47:43.658
Detective Edmonds, Meg said.

00:47:43.718 --> 00:47:46.049
Did the hospital call?

00:47:46.109 --> 00:47:49.651
Is Craig going to be all right?

00:47:49.711 --> 00:47:53.873
Winter's, Detective Edmonds said.

00:47:53.933 --> 00:47:58.436
Yes, he's going to be okay.

00:47:58.496 --> 00:48:01.768
Can I call the hospital now?"

00:48:01.828 --> 00:48:03.649
asked Meg.

00:48:03.709 --> 00:48:07.780
I'd like you to wait, said Edmonds.

00:48:07.840 --> 00:48:11.931
Detective Keet is going to be here in a minute.

00:48:11.991 --> 00:48:19.032
He's just coming from the airport, and he looked through the open door.

00:48:19.092 --> 00:48:20.203
Ah!

00:48:20.263 --> 00:48:22.826
Here he is now.

00:48:22.886 --> 00:48:32.804
A second detective came into the room, and behind him was a tall man with dark hair.

00:48:32.864 --> 00:48:36.036
Meg stood up quickly.

00:48:36.096 --> 00:48:39.228
Daddy, she cried.

00:48:39.288 --> 00:48:42.501
What are you doing here?

00:48:42.561 --> 00:48:50.772
The police called me, said Howard Hudson, and I flew here at once.

00:48:50.832 --> 00:48:55.171
Detective Keet met me at the airport.

00:48:55.231 --> 00:48:58.162
Now sit down, Meg.

00:48:58.223 --> 00:49:01.094
I want you to listen to me."

00:49:01.154 --> 00:49:05.116
He did not look at Nick.

00:49:05.176 --> 00:49:11.148
Meg sat down, and her father took her hands.

00:49:11.208 --> 00:49:18.474
Meg, last week Johnny Vickers came to my house.

00:49:18.534 --> 00:49:22.096
He wanted to talk about his daughter.

00:49:22.156 --> 00:49:25.810
You remember Anna, Meg?

00:49:25.870 --> 00:49:34.196
Three months ago, she jumped off a bridge in Boston and died.

00:49:34.256 --> 00:49:42.264
She was young, beautiful, rich, and she didn't want to live.

00:49:42.324 --> 00:49:44.266
Why?

00:49:44.326 --> 00:49:53.800
Because she loved a man, and the man took her money, ran away, and left her.

00:49:53.860 --> 00:49:57.751
And the man was called, No!

00:49:57.811 --> 00:49:59.992
said Meg.

00:50:00.012 --> 00:50:00.752
No!

00:50:00.812 --> 00:50:02.843
Yes, Meg.

00:50:02.903 --> 00:50:04.514
Yes.

00:50:04.574 --> 00:50:10.502
He was called Mr. Hollywood.

00:50:10.562 --> 00:50:13.562
shouted Meg.

00:50:13.622 --> 00:50:16.373
She began to cry.

00:50:16.434 --> 00:50:23.098
That's right, Miss Hudson, said Detective Keet quietly.

00:50:23.158 --> 00:50:28.534
To you, he gave the name Craig Winters.

00:50:28.594 --> 00:50:34.237
When Anna Vickers knew him, he was Carl Windsor.

00:50:34.298 --> 00:50:43.614
But he liked all his, uh, girl friends, to call him Mr. Hollywood.

00:50:43.674 --> 00:50:53.670
He took nearly fifty thousand dollars from Anna Vickers, and there was a girl before that.

00:50:53.730 --> 00:50:55.320
No!

00:50:55.380 --> 00:50:57.642
It's not true!

00:50:57.702 --> 00:50:59.462
Meg shouted.

00:50:59.522 --> 00:51:03.695
It is true, Meg, said her father.

00:51:03.755 --> 00:51:10.670
Winters, Windsor, gets all his money from rich men's daughters.

00:51:10.730 --> 00:51:14.142
Johnny Vickers loved his daughter.

00:51:14.202 --> 00:51:18.786
He went to her house in Boston after she died.

00:51:18.846 --> 00:51:26.840
He read her letters and learned about the money and the name, Mr. Hollywood.

00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:33.326
And when he came to my house, I told him about you, Meg.

00:51:33.386 --> 00:51:42.713
I said, my daughter's got a new boyfriend, and she calls him Mr. Hollywood.

00:51:42.773 --> 00:51:47.365
I don't like him, but I can't stop her.

00:51:47.425 --> 00:51:51.527
She's going away to meet him next week, I think.

00:51:51.587 --> 00:51:53.837
What can I do?

00:51:53.898 --> 00:52:02.802
Johnny put his hand on my arm, and he said, don't be afraid for your daughter.

00:52:02.862 --> 00:52:09.598
I'm going to find that man and stop him.

00:52:09.658 --> 00:52:13.334
Meg said nothing.

00:52:13.394 --> 00:52:16.757
Her face was very white.

00:52:16.818 --> 00:52:21.171
For a minute or two, nobody spoke.

00:52:21.231 --> 00:52:29.118
Then Detective Edmonds said, Vickers told us all about it, Miss Hudson.

00:52:29.178 --> 00:52:34.052
He followed you to Whistler and saw you with...

00:52:34.112 --> 00:52:41.000
Nick began to understand with me in the cafe.

00:52:41.060 --> 00:52:45.414
and Meg called me, Mr. Hollywood."

00:52:45.474 --> 00:52:49.414
Howard Hudson looked at Nick.

00:52:49.474 --> 00:52:53.885
You're the travel writer guy, right?

00:52:53.945 --> 00:52:55.716
Lorts.

00:52:55.776 --> 00:52:59.416
Nick Lorts, said Nick.

00:52:59.476 --> 00:53:02.257
Vickers nearly killed me.

00:53:02.317 --> 00:53:05.647
He shot at me twice, and…

00:53:05.707 --> 00:53:10.408
But Howard Hudson was not very interested in Nick.

00:53:10.468 --> 00:53:13.938
He looked at his daughter again.

00:53:13.998 --> 00:53:18.121
How much money did you give him, Meg?

00:53:18.181 --> 00:53:28.517
He said, I, I gave him $25,000.

00:53:28.577 --> 00:53:33.020
Said Meg, only for two or three months.

00:53:33.080 --> 00:53:40.313
He said, then he, she began to cry again.

00:53:40.373 --> 00:53:47.665
"'Well, you can say goodbye to that money,' said Hudson angrily.

00:53:47.685 --> 00:53:52.326
"'What's going to happen to Vickers?'

00:53:52.386 --> 00:53:54.747
Nick asked Detective Edmonds.

00:53:54.767 --> 00:53:59.449
"'Hospital, I think,' said Edmonds.

00:53:59.469 --> 00:54:10.807
"'Okay, he shot at you, and about fifty people saw him, but he's not a well man.

00:54:10.867 --> 00:54:16.844
The doctors are going to put him away in a hospital.

00:54:16.904 --> 00:54:20.425
Howard Hudson stood up.

00:54:20.485 --> 00:54:22.736
Okay, Meg.

00:54:22.796 --> 00:54:25.257
I'm going to take you home.

00:54:25.317 --> 00:54:29.743
My plane is waiting at the airport.

00:54:29.803 --> 00:54:33.740
Meg followed her father to the door.

00:54:33.800 --> 00:54:37.762
Then she remembered Nick, and turned.

00:54:37.822 --> 00:54:40.884
I'm sorry, she said.

00:54:40.944 --> 00:54:43.856
I got you into all this.

00:54:43.917 --> 00:54:47.438
I called you Mr. Hollywood.

00:54:47.498 --> 00:54:49.530
That was wrong.

00:54:49.590 --> 00:54:51.911
But I didn't know.

00:54:51.972 --> 00:54:54.984
It's okay, said Nick.

00:54:55.044 --> 00:54:58.016
You know everything now.

00:54:58.076 --> 00:55:00.918
And it's better to learn it now.

00:55:00.978 --> 00:55:02.238
and not later.

00:55:02.258 --> 00:55:07.909
$50,000 later.

00:55:07.970 --> 00:55:14.661
Chapter 8 A nice smile.

00:55:14.721 --> 00:55:20.042
Nick took the evening ferry back to Vancouver.

00:55:20.102 --> 00:55:28.048
He was tired and hungry, so he went down to get some dinner in the ferry restaurant.

00:55:28.108 --> 00:55:34.136
The restaurant was busy, and there was only one free table.

00:55:34.196 --> 00:55:39.230
Nick sat down quickly, and began to eat.

00:55:39.290 --> 00:55:49.807
I must get back to work tomorrow, he thought, and forget about millionaire's daughters and men with guns.

00:55:49.827 --> 00:55:55.912
"'Excuse me,' somebody said.

00:55:55.972 --> 00:55:58.692
Can I sit with you?

00:55:58.752 --> 00:56:01.312
Nick looked up.

00:56:01.372 --> 00:56:06.004
There was a pretty girl next to his table.

00:56:06.064 --> 00:56:09.598
He got up.

00:56:09.658 --> 00:56:12.880
It's okay, he said.

00:56:12.940 --> 00:56:15.402
You can have this table.

00:56:15.462 --> 00:56:17.352
I don't want it.

00:56:17.412 --> 00:56:20.645
And he began to move away.

00:56:20.705 --> 00:56:23.206
Please don't go.

00:56:23.266 --> 00:56:25.098
The girl said.

00:56:25.158 --> 00:56:28.532
Stay and finish your dinner.

00:56:28.592 --> 00:56:31.374
She smiled at him.

00:56:31.435 --> 00:56:34.277
It was a nice smile.

00:56:34.337 --> 00:56:39.592
But Nick knew all about nice smiles.

00:56:39.652 --> 00:56:47.648
I'm not hungry, he said, and he walked quickly out of the restaurant.

